/* ===========================================================================
   QUILLMOOR ACADEMY · THE OBSERVATORY — guide-content.js  (12 Nov 2026)
   The hand-written scripts for the Scriptorium's High and Medium guidance.
   One script per chart; the first (the test run) is p-line-museums.
   Contract and shapes: docs/GUIDANCE-LEVELS.md.

   A step:
     id      unique in the script
     label   the decision, two or three words (shown as the step name)
     ask     the question
     ok      the right option: it is also the text that goes into the pane
     wrong   [[option, hint], …]  three wrong options, each with its own hint.
             A hint says what kind of thing is wrong; it never gives the answer.
     pre     what the engine puts before the text in the pane (default ' ';
             nothing for the first step of a pane)
     post    what the engine puts after it (',' or '.' …)
     shape   Medium: what to type, in a few words
     expect  Medium: the expected value, in words, sent to the AI check
     accept  Medium, rule check: every group must match one alternative
             (regular-expression source, case-insensitive)
     reject  Medium, rule check: known slips, each with its hint
     hint, hint2   Medium: the first and the second hint
     tag     the fault tag (content.js REMEDIATION) a miss is counted under

   The essay that all the right options make is checked in tools/guide-test.js:
   every figure against the chart, 160–190 words, no red or amber Ward.
   =========================================================================== */
